 r"I am writing to apply for the 2027 Graduate Development Programme in Advisory at WSP, in the Digital Advisory team in London. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have helped organisations use data and digital tools to make better decisions, and turned the results into dashboards, tools and recommendations that people actually use.",

 r"What attracts me most to Digital Advisory is that the work has a visible end point: digital strategies, dashboards and reporting tools that change how a hospital, an infrastructure owner or an environmental programme actually runs. The posting describes helping clients use data, technology and digital ways of working to solve real-world challenges, and seeing how digital ideas become meaningful outcomes, which is the part of my work I have enjoyed most. I like taking an unclear problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a campaign for merchants by hand, I worked through a few examples, saw the underlying logic and used Claude Code to build a multi-step agent with a validation step to check its own output, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent. Persuading a sceptical colleague that it was accurate was harder than building it, and it taught me that a digital solution only creates value once the people using it trust it.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing healthcare AI engagement for a pharmaceutical client. I worked with the client's clinical experts to turn their safety requirements into a 246-question benchmark and rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, built the Python pipeline that tested the product against it, and presented the findings and risks to clinical and business stakeholders. It showed me how much of advisory work is agreeing what good looks like with the client before any analysis starts.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants to model cardiovascular risk and was delivered as an interactive Streamlit tool, so that non-specialists could explore the results without touching the code. At Ipsos Strategy3 I researched emerging health-product markets, built market-sizing models and presented recommendations to clients. Both taught me to present a finding to an audience who wants the implication rather than the method, which I would bring to WSP's health and environment clients.",

 r"I would bring WSP strong data and digital skills in Python, SQL and dashboarding, experience building practical AI-enabled tools, a background in healthcare and life sciences, and the habit of explaining technical work clearly to clients. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship. I am based in London and available to start in September 2027.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in data, digital tools and client delivery could contribute to WSP's Digital Advisory team.",
